+-- ─── View-size lever (bench variant only) ────────────────────────
+--
+-- The ONE difference between this app and `examples/19-skyforum`.
+-- `FORUM_POSTS` (default 5, the stock seed count) sets how many posts
+-- the home page renders, so ONE binary produces every view size in the
+-- fixed-term regression. Varying N by editing a literal list would
+-- vary the binary too, and a fitted intercept is only meaningful if
+-- the code under it is identical at every point.
+--
+-- The lever is in `init` only. Nothing on the interaction path reads
+-- it: `view`, `update` and every `View/*` module are byte-identical to
+-- the stock example.
+benchPostCount : Int
+benchPostCount =
+    Maybe.withDefault
+        5
+        (String.toInt (System.getenvOr "FORUM_POSTS" "5"))
+
+
+-- FORUM_POSTS = 5 is the stock seed and reproduces `examples/19-skyforum`
+-- exactly (94 sky-id elements, 135 tags). ABOVE 5 the seed is extended;
+-- BELOW 5 it is truncated, down to 0 posts / 14 elements of page chrome.
+--
+-- The small sizes exist so the regression INTERPOLATES its intercept
+-- instead of extrapolating it. Extrapolating a fixed term from two points
+-- at 94 and 384 elements -- which is what the showcase figure did -- puts
+-- the intercept 94 elements outside the data, where a mild superlinearity
+-- in the slope shows up as a large change in the constant.
+benchPosts : List Post -> List Post
+benchPosts seeded =
+    if benchPostCount < List.length seeded then
+        List.take benchPostCount seeded
+
+    else if benchPostCount == List.length seeded then
+        seeded
+
+    else
+        seeded ++ List.map benchPost (List.range 6 benchPostCount)
+
+
+-- Title length is held constant across N. Per-post element count is
+-- structural and does not depend on it, but per-post BYTES would, and
+-- a term that grows with N for a reason other than element count would
+-- contaminate the slope.
+benchPost : Int -> Post
+benchPost i =
+    Post
+        i
+        ("Bench post "
+            ++ String.fromInt i
+            ++ " — a link-aggregator headline of typical length")
+        ("https://example.com/bench/" ++ String.fromInt i)
+        "alice"
+        (100 + i)
+        3
+        []
+        []
